TITLE:: PltWavesets
summary:: The signal cut at zero crossings: pitch and peak per waveset, and one drawn large
categories:: Libraries>PlotLib
related:: Overviews/PlotLib, Classes/PltWave, Classes/PltNovelty

DESCRIPTION::
Three panels sharing a time axis: the pitch each waveset implies, its peak, and the
chosen waveset at its own scale. A waveset is a shape, and the shapes differ wildly
inside one sound, which is the whole reason for waveset synthesis.

The segmentation follows the Wavesets quark exactly, so the two agree: a crossing is
a move from non-positive to positive, a waveset runs from one crossing to the next,
and code::minLength:: suppresses the ones too short to be a cycle. The test suite
cross checks against the quark when it is installed.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: signal
argument:: sampleRate
argument:: minLength
Shortest waveset in samples. 10 is the quark's default, which puts the ceiling
around 4.4 kHz.
argument:: title
argument:: width
argument:: height

METHOD:: fromSoundFile
One channel of a file.
argument:: path
argument:: channel
argument:: maxFrames
Caps what is held in memory for the detail panel.
argument:: minLength
argument:: title
argument:: width
argument:: height

METHOD:: segments
The wavesets of a signal: code::(xings:, fracXings:, lengths:, amps:)::, named as
the quark names them. code::fracXings:: interpolate the crossing between the two
samples that straddle it, so a length is not quantised. code::amps:: is the peak
magnitude of each waveset, positive or negative, whichever is larger.

METHOD:: frequencies
The pitch each length implies. A waveset is one cycle by definition, so its length
is a period.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: select
Which waveset the detail panel draws, by index.
METHOD:: selectAt
The same, by time in seconds.
METHOD:: wavesetAt
The samples of one waveset.
METHOD:: frequencies
METHOD:: xings
METHOD:: fracXings
METHOD:: lengths
METHOD:: amps
METHOD:: signal
METHOD:: sampleRate
METHOD:: duration
METHOD:: selected
METHOD:: minHz
METHOD:: maxHz
Range of the pitch panel, which is logarithmic.
METHOD:: panelGap
METHOD:: pitchColorKey
METHOD:: ampColorKey
METHOD:: traceColorKey

EXAMPLES::
code::
// speech, where the pitch trace and the noisy consonants separate clearly
(
w = PltWavesets.fromSoundFile(Platform.resourceDir +/+ "sounds/a11wlk01.wav").front;
w.selectAt(0.85);
)

// a sine: every waveset the same length, the pitch a flat line
(
PltWavesets(Signal.fill(48000, { |i| sin(i * 2pi * 220 / 48000) * 0.8 }),
	48000, 10, "220 Hz").front;
)

// step through the wavesets and watch the shape change
(
Routine({ 200.do { |i| w.select(600 + i); 0.08.wait } }).play(AppClock);
)

// data only
(
var seg = PltWavesets.segments(Signal.fill(10000, { |i| sin(i * 2pi / 100) }), 10);
[seg[\lengths].mean, PltWavesets.frequencies(seg[\lengths], 48000).mean];
)
::
